// BUG-ZYB-005 — a function DEFINED IN a module, handed to another module.
//
// The mirror image of lambda_alias_cruzando.zy, and the pair is the finding:
// each Rust engine broke a different one of the three ways to pass a function
// between modules, so for a while there was no way to write a higher-order
// call across modules that ran on both.
//
// The VM answered `'_mas_uno' is undefined — did you mean '_mas_uno°'?`,
// pointing at hot definitions, which have nothing to do with it. Calling a
// private sibling worked and passing it did not: the compiler consulted
// `module_scope` when compiling a call and not when compiling the same name as
// a value.
//
// Found by packaging, not by running: a `.zyp` defaults to `--vm`, so the first
// run of the package was the first time the line met the VM at all.
<# ./pasador => p

>> "fn de módulo cruzando: " p::prueba() ¶
